    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on thompson1917-ch13-11: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.49";
    dc:description "The proposed mechanical couple yields a clean controlled test. Public observational plant records do not contain the force, adhesion and torsion measurements needed to distinguish it from adaptive or developmental alternatives.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Compare genetically and developmentally matched stems twining on supports differing only in calibrated roughness, measuring adhesion, torque and stem torsion over time. Torsion scaling with adhesion-generated torque supports the claim; equal torsion on smooth supports or no torque-torsion link refutes it.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Support roughness also changes contact geometry and plant behavior.", "The required controlled rough-versus-smooth time series is not known as a reusable public dataset.";
